- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests`

**How to implement.** The wizard's view, under stable ids (001 §K: preview, column roles, the profile picker; 001 §O 'Automation: every new control gets a stable id'; .spec-md §10.5: Attach and Cancel share a row with a gap and distinct colours; AGENTS.md: a WrapPanel never sits in a horizontal StackPanel). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs` (step 308): `importWizardView (m : ImportWizardModel) (dispatch : ImportWizardMsg -> unit) : IView` is a `DockPanel`. Docked at the bottom is one horizontal row of `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton ConstructorUiId.importWizardAttachButton (ControlCaption "Attach") positiveBackground`, present only while the source read, and `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importWizardCancelButton (ControlCaption "Cancel") negativeBackground` (step 107's look), sending `ApplyImportWizard` and `CancelImportWizard`. Above it a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importWizardMessage` shows `lastError`'s caption, or `The file could not be read — <e.describe>` while the source is an error, in `messageColor`, and is absent otherwise. Docked at the top, in a vertical `StackPanel`: a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importWizardHeading` with `Import <the file's leaf name>` and the line `Nothing is attached until you press Attach.`; a `Layout:` block whose `WrapPanel` holds one box per `DataDelimiter.all` (`importWizardDelimiterChoice delimiter.uiKey`, sending `SetImportDelimiter`) and one per header choice (`importWizardHeaderChoice header.uiKey`, sending `SetImportHeader`), the chosen ones `actionButton`s on `positiveBackground` and the others `verbButton`s, and a `TextBlock` carrying `importWizardBomText` with the mark's caption; a `Profile:` block whose `WrapPanel` holds one box per built-in, in `BuiltInImportProfile.all` order, and per kit profile, in the kit's order, each carrying `importWizardProfileChoice name.uiKey` with the name as its label and sending `PickImportProfile`, then `New column mapping` carrying `importWizardNewMappingButton` and sending `StartColumnMapping`, the chosen one on `positiveBackground`; and, under `NewColumnMapping`, a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Profile name:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `importWizardProfileNameField` that shows `profileName` and sends `SetImportProfileName` at every change. A `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways fills the rest and holds a `Grid` carrying `importWizardPreviewGrid`, one column per preview column: its first row the column's name; under `NewColumnMapping` a second row holding, per column, a `ComboBox` carrying `importWizardColumnRoleChoice column.uiPosition` whose items are the roles' captions (`UnmappedColumnRole`, `ScanColumnRole (DegreeColumnUnit, PhysicalScanValue)`, `SignalColumnRole`, `SigmaColumnRole`, `TimestampColumnRole`, `CaptureIndexColumnRole`, `ObservableColumnRole`, `KeyColumnRole`, `ThroughputColumnRole` and `MuellerElementRole` of each `MuellerElementIndex.all`), the column's role selected (any scan role at the scan item), sending `SetColumnRole`; and, for a column whose role is a scan role, two more `ComboBox`es carrying `importWizardColumnUnitChoice` (`ScanColumnUnit.all`) and `importWizardColumnReadingChoice` (`ScanReading.all`) that send `SetColumnRole` with the new unit or reading; then one row per preview row, a `TextBlock` per cell. A preview error shows its caption in place of the grid. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type DataDelimiter with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`comma`, `semicolon`, `tab`); `type HeaderRowChoice with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`first-row`, `no-header`) and `member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`First row is a header`, `No header row`); `type DataDelimiter with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Comma`, `Semicolon`, `Tab`); `type ByteOrderMark with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Byte-order mark: yes`, `Byte-order mark: no`); `type ImportProfileName with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` and `member this.caption : ControlCaption`, both its text; `type DataColumnNumber with member this.uiPosition : ConstructorUiPosition`, its value; `type ImportProfileError with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its `describe`; `type ColumnRoleChoice with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its `text` (`scan variable` for every scan role); `type ScanColumnUnit with member this.caption : ControlCaption` and `type ScanReading with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, their texts. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a group after the import dialog's (step 107), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S9.2, each with a one-line doc: `importWizardWindow` (`"ImportWizardWindow"`), `importWizardHeading` (`"ImportWizardHeading"`), `importWizardDelimiterChoice (delimiter : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"ImportWizardDelimiter_{delimiter.value}"`), `importWizardHeaderChoice (header : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"ImportWizardHeader_{header.value}"`), `importWizardBomText` (`"ImportWizardBomText"`), `importWizardProfileChoice (profile : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"ImportWizardProfile_{profile.value}"`), `importWizardNewMappingButton` (`"ImportWizardNewMappingButton"`), `importWizardProfileNameField` (`"ImportWizardProfileNameField"`), `importWizardPreviewGrid` (`"ImportWizardPreviewGrid"`), `importWizardColumnRoleChoice (column : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$"ImportWizardColumnRole_{column.value}"`), `importWizardColumnUnitChoice (column : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$"ImportWizardColumnUnit_{column.value}"`), `importWizardColumnReadingChoice (column : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$"ImportWizardColumnReading_{column.value}"`), `importWizardMessage` (`"ImportWizardMessage"`), `importWizardAttachButton` (`"ImportWizardAttachButton"`), `importWizardCancelButton` (`"ImportWizardCancelButton"`). No other id is added. Tests, in `ImportWizardTests` (step 308): `the import wizard UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the fifteen ids' texts, the parameterised ones over `comma`, `Phone ROI CSV` and position 4. `the wizard shows the sniffed layout, every profile and the preview, with Attach and Cancel in one row`: `importWizardView` over the class's opened model, mounted headless as `ImportDialogTests` mounts the import dialog's view (step 107), shows the heading naming the file, the comma choice on the positive background, the byte-order-mark caption, profile choices for the four built-ins and `Lab scan` and `importWizardNewMappingButton`, and the preview grid holding the five column names and both rows' cells; `importWizardAttachButton` and `importWizardCancelButton` have equal tops, Cancel to the right of Attach with a gap between them. `a new column mapping shows a role per column, and a scan role its unit and reading`: after `StartColumnMapping` and `SetColumnRole` of column 4 to a scan role, the grid holds a role choice for each of the five columns and a unit and a reading choice for column 4 alone, and `importWizardProfileNameField` is present; before it, neither is. `a refused Attach shows its reason in the wizard`: after Attach with an empty name, `importWizardMessage` shows `the import profile name is blank`.

**Acceptance.** After the view lands, `importWizardView` MUST show the heading, the layout choices and the mark, every profile, the preview grid with a role per column under a new mapping, and Attach and Cancel in one row, under the fifteen stable `ConstructorUiId` members; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import wizard UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the wizard shows the sniffed layout, every profile and the preview, with Attach and Cancel in one row`, `a new column mapping shows a role per column, and a scan role its unit and reading` and `a refused Attach shows its reason in the wizard`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
